## 5. TFFL: Trustworthy & Fair FL (IEEE TIFS 2025)
**Core Mechanism:** Uses Subjective Logic (SL) to calculate reputation with Time Decay (DSL). Uses Cooperative Game Theory to distribute incentives.
**Comparison to Ours:** Validates our use of temporal tracking (**EMA**) to prevent attackers from gaming the system across rounds.

### Quantitative Performance Metrics:
**Datasets:** MNIST, CIFAR-10
**Attacks Tested:** Label-flipping, Sybil, Backdoor.
**Key Results (FL Convergence Accuracy & Bandwidth):**
- **Accuracy on MNIST (Non-IID):**
  - **DRC (TFFL):** $\approx 91\%$
  - **PBFL / FedAvg:** $\approx 90\%$ / $87\%$
- **Accuracy on CIFAR-10 (Non-IID):**
  - **DRC (TFFL):** $\approx 84\%$
  - **FedAvg / PBFL:** $80\% - 81\%$
- **Bandwidth Usage:** DRC reduced average bandwidth usage by 10-25% on CIFAR-10 compared to PBFL.
*Takeaway:* Temporal reputation tracking strictly improves global convergence accuracy by 3-4% over standard FedAvg in Non-IID environments while keeping resource overhead manageable.

